    "introduction": "A versatile theatre actress, Paula's breakthrough television role came in playing the fierce-willed character of Donna in the BBC's long running continuing drama \"Eastenders\".This has led to a diverse variety of television roles that have demonstrated Paula's versatility. From an ambitious police Detective Inspector (\"Silent Witness\"), to a comical trophy wife (\"Midsomer Murders\"); and a tragically-romantic World War 2 \"Land Girl\" (\"Foyle's War\"), to a cunningly-manipulative fortune hunter (\"To The Ends Of The Earth\"), Paula has become a familiar face on British network television.Paula continues to split her time between television and theater productions. In the 2007 touring theater production of Mike Leigh's \"Abigail's Party\", Paula was nominated for the prestigious MEN (Manchester Evening News) Award for Best Actress, in the iconic role of Beverly.Paula currently resides in London, England.- IMDb mini biography by: Peter Briggs",
